        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): trigger model fallback on usage-limit promptError (#103734)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a Codex-backed turn hits the subscription usage limit, the Codex harness\nreturns a `promptError` in the attempt result instead of throwing. The host's\nmodel fallback is throw-driven — it only engages when `FailoverError` is\nthrown. As a result, the configured fallback model is never tried and the run\nfails terminally.\n\nFixes #103734.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo changes in the embedded agent runner:\n\n1. **`run.ts`**: when `promptError` text is classified as `rate_limit` or\n   `billing` by the canonical `classifyFailoverReason`, mark the incomplete\n   turn as `fallbackSafe` and preserve the original error text in\n   `meta.error.message`.\n\n2. **`result-fallback-classifier.ts`**: detect rate/usage limit messages in\n   `meta.error.message` via `classifyFailoverReason` (before the generic\n   incomplete-turn handler) and classify them as `rate_limit`, so the\n   fallback loop switches to the configured fallback.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Codex usage limit → terminal failure, fallback model never tried\n**After:** Codex usage limit → `rate_limit` failover → falls back to next\nconfigured model (e.g. `anthropic/claude-opus-4-8`)\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/103734-codex-usage-limit-fallback` | Base: `upstream/main`\n\n### Live model proof\n\nNormal agent run completes successfully:\n\n```\n$ pnpm --filter openclaw openclaw agent --local --model zte/Qwen3-235B-A22B --message \"say hello in one word\" --session-key agent:default:proof-103734\n\n[model-fetch] status=200 model=Qwen3-235B-A22B elapsedMs=5477\nhello\n[agent] run ended with stopReason=stop\n```\n\n### End-to-end classifier proof\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof/codex-usage-limit-fallback.mts\n\nCase 1 — usage limit → rate_limit: PASS\nCase 2 — rate limit message → rate_limit: PASS\nCase 3 — generic message → not rate_limit: PASS\nCase 4 — quota exceeded → rate_limit: PASS\nCase 5 — non-rate-limit → not rate_limit: PASS\n\nOVERALL: ALL PASSED\n```\n\n### Regression tests\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/result-fallback-classifier.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  20 passed (20)\n```\n\n### Pre-submit checks\n\n```\noxfmt --check → All matched files use the correct format\noxlint        → 0 errors\ngit diff --check → clean\nautoreview    → clean — patch is correct (0.95)\n```\n\n### Diff summary\n\n```\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/result-fallback-classifier.ts | 23 +++++\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run.ts                        | 28 ++++-\nscripts/proof/codex-usage-limit-fallback.mts                   | 95 ++++++++\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
        "branch": "fix/103734-codex-usage-limit-fallback",
        "head_sha": "4cc3c2e6733de761681c07368e57fc20af802c10",
